    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 4th slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** as the day\u2019s premier asset. With an elite efficiency score of 82.13, he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Leahy (4.52 xERA) and a 10% boost for hitting at the top of the order, making him our primary engine for both AVG and the scarce SB category. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (74.33) despite a minor BvP tax; his matchup against Kelly (5.47 xERA) and a massive 19% SP skill advantage position him to provide high-leverage production. We are also tracking **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** closely; while both hold strong scores near 67, their exposure to a 40% rain risk in their respective matchups necessitates a contingency plan if starters are pulled early.\n\nOur bench composition was dictated by efficiency margins, with **Luke Raley** representing the most difficult exclusion. Scoring 58.60, **Luke Raley** was a viable candidate, but he was ultimately benched in favor of higher-projected starters like **Yordan Alvarez**\u2014who, despite a challenging matchup against Rasmussen, maintains an elite 0.477 xwOBA that cannot be ignored. We opted to minimize exposure against elite arms today, which is why **Kazuma Okamoto** (42.90) is barely clinging to a start against Gilbert; his scoring floor is significantly lower than the remainder of our lineup, yet he remains in the utility slot due to the lack of a superior bench alternative. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, **Chase Meidroth**, and **Carson Benge**, all of whom fall into the \"Below Floor\" or marginal categories today, reinforcing our strategy to preserve game caps until more favorable pitching environments emerge for our depth pieces.",
